Z||000006||Oreif||12-03-2001||03:00 PM||||First, Who is "they"?<BR>The REAL Indy Pace car is by far the fastest and lightest that Pontiac assisted in building. (Note: where more than one was built and the cars are still around today) Archie builds some nice V-8's.<BR>There are quite a few 3.4L, 3800sc, and Northstar builders. <BR>As for stock from the factory, The 85 GT is the lightest with a V-6. The 88 Formula is only 50 lbs more but has a better ratio 5-spd for higher top end. (I think they were about the same 0-60) 88's have redesigned suspension and vented brakes. 84-87 parts are slightly less expensive than 88's.<P>I think FieroMaster88 says it best.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">           <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
