Z||000010||BlackStang95||12-03-2001||03:21 PM||||The best in the world in my opinion is that blue lt1 chop top.  The best stock I'd say is the 88 gt.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroclub.cjb.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroclub.cjb.net/</A> <BR>click on models and years, it shows the differences.<P>The maitnance is comparable to other mid 80s cars, although its harder to do some routine stuff yourself (spark plug wires were a nightmare).<p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Pyric||12-03-2001||05:43 PM||||The question is... best in what way? I personally like them all, but I prefer the V6 and I like the notchback with the spoiler.  <P>Now, I'd also like a T-Top... But I don't think they made a GT notchback with one.<P>Would have been sweet though.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> <P>The 88's are nice performance-wise... and I'd like to have one... But when I picture a fiero in my mind it's from the first few years.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fformula88||12-03-2001||05:55 PM||||The best Fiero you can buy is whatever year and model that you can find in really good shape.  Your preferences may steer you to the GT fastback design, or the notchbacks.  4 Cyl's or V6.  The different options, colors etc.  However, since they are older cars and often have a lot of milage (almost always) then whatever one you can find that has been well taken care of, is in good shape, and everything works might be the best one to get.  regardless of year/body style or model!||||reg||1
